{"role":"assistant","content":"Fixed the notification-handler bug in `bin/nightly-review.zsh:19`.\n\nTwo causes were found:\n\n- Claude was exiting with `Not logged in · Please run /login`, so no summaries were produced.\n- The script then assigned to `status`, a read-only special variable in zsh. That aborted the script before `notify.sh` could send a failure message.\n\nThe variable is now named `exit_code`. Local tests using stand-ins for Claude and Telegram verified both success and failure notification paths, output creation, exit-code preservation, and script syntax. No external services were contacted.\n\nFull details are in `ANSWER.md`. Successful reviews still require Claude authentication in the launchd user’s environment; that login was not available or attempted here."}
